Short:        WebKit web browser for AmigaOS 3.2 (68040+FPU)
Author:       AmigaChrome Team
Uploader:     UPLOADER-PLACEHOLDER
Type:         comm/www
Version:      0.8
Architecture: m68k-amigaos >= 3.2
Distribution: Aminet

OpenBrowser is a web browser for AmigaOS 3.2 built on WebKit: WebCore lays
out and draws real web pages, and JavaScriptCore runs their JavaScript with
the Team's 68k template JIT. Pages are fetched with HTTP/2 and https
(OpenTLS), pictures are decoded by the system's datatypes, and pages seen
before load from a disk cache.

This is a test version (0.8 test, 22 October 2026). Things will still go
wrong; reports are welcome.

Installing
----------
Double-click Install-OpenBrowser (the Installer). It checks for AmigaOS 3.2
and a 68040 or 68060 with its FPU, asks where the OpenBrowser drawer goes
(about 195 MB; Work: rather than System:), and adds only what is missing or
too old: opentls.library 1.2+, opencrypto.library 2.1+, json.library, and
the certificates in S:OpenTLS. With webbrowser.library installed, the
installed engine is kept as LIBS:WebBrowser/WebBrowserEngine.before-20261022
and LIBS:WebBrowser/WebBrowserEngine becomes a small script that runs the
new engine in the drawer. Nothing is deleted. Novice, Intermediate and
Expert levels, pretend mode and the log all work.

From a Shell instead: CD into the OpenBrowser drawer and type
Execute Install.

Reboot after installing, then double-click OpenBrowser.

Requirements
------------
- AmigaOS 3.2 or newer
- a 68040 or 68060 with its FPU (hard float; not an LC or EC CPU)
- about 120 MB of free Fast RAM
- a TCP/IP stack with bsdsocket.library (OpenSocket or another)

Undo
----
Delete the OpenBrowser drawer. If webbrowser.library was installed, delete
the small script LIBS:WebBrowser/WebBrowserEngine and rename
WebBrowserEngine.before-20261022 back to WebBrowserEngine. Libraries kept as
*.before-20261022 in LIBS: can be renamed back the same way. The Installer's
log, Install-OpenBrowser.log in the drawer, lists everything it did.

